  "manual": [
    "Lines that need a war: a state and a victory point taken with the general on the spot, capitulation, landings",
    "A landing and an airborne drop with the honour switches on: the lines in the divisions' history",
    "A peace conference that hands states over (whether has_war_with still holds then), a civil war won, a government in exile"
  ],
  "checklist": [
    "The title strip and the tabs as before: Germany's flag, Records, German Reich, 'Kept since 1 January, 1936 - 0 days on record'; the War Diary's tab with the gold chevrons; each tab opens its page",
    "The list: no row of its own for a day; the date (hoi_16mbs) stands on a day's first line only, every line of a day on one band, the bands of two days apart; 'The record begins' on the lighter band of a new line until the window is closed once, then on the day's band",
    "Close and open the Records after a day with a line: the new lines on the lighter band (GFX_1440p_SG_pick); does it read as 'new' against the day bands?",
    "A line about a country (mod1440_chk_war: War declared on Poland): its flag (41x26) and name; click the name: the diary shows Poland's lines only, 'Poland: lines 1 - N of N' in the head bar where Officer stood, the Country and Officer heads gone, no filter lit; All brings every line back",
    "A state taken in battle (mod1440_chk_war, then mod1440_chk_state2: Danzig): 'State taken', the plate moves the camera, Poland in the Country column, the general's face and name at the right; click his name: the Officers page opens on his file",
    "A state received by treaty (mod1440_chk_treaty): 'Received from' Austria in the diary (Territory filter too), no general named; the state card of Niederschlesien: 'Received from Austria by treaty on 1 January, 1936, held 0 days' and the grey line that no troops are named; 'Handed over to' Austria for the state given first",
    "A run of states (mod1440_chk_treaty_run: four states received from Austria on one day): All shows one row 'Received from <state>' with '+3 states' at the plate's right end and its tooltip; Territory lists the four lines; 'lines 1 - N of M' counts the four",
    "An officer line (mod1440_chk_level: a general gains a skill level): 'Gained a skill level' with the level reached in yellow at the right end of the words (compare with the level in the general's own window); his face and name open his file",
    "mod1440_chk_retire (the fifth general retires), then mod1440_chk_daily: 'Left the service' with his face and name; The service: Left the service 1. A second mod1440_chk_daily writes no second line",
    "mod1440_chk_cipher and mod1440_chk_exile: 'Broke the cipher of' Poland and 'Hosting the exiled government of' Poland, each with its flag (volunteers, a civil war won and fighting on need a war the check cannot cause: under manual)",
    "The pane: The campaign as banded tables under three head bars (War and peace, Ground in battle with taken and lost and a bar, the By treaty row, The service); 'At war today' equals the number of enemies on the Wars page; Wars begun and Wars ended against the Wars page's rows",
    "The chronicle: mark three lines with their boxes: the pane lists the newest marked lines (date in grey, icon, words, name); 'Read the chronicle' opens the Marked filter; unmark them all: the two lines that say how to mark",
    "Battle honours: the four switches in two rows toggle; By themselves and Cited by you as a table row; the last citation under them",
    "Kept: two lines; the count in the head bar has the Kept text as its tooltip",
    "The page arrows past 200 rows (mod1440_chk_fill fills the logs): 200 lines a page with no day rows; 'lines 1 - 200 of M'; scroll the list to its end; mod1440_chk_list_time in game.log (the folds' cost against the last check)",
    "The top bar button: a War and peace line written while the window is closed turns the count red; its tooltip says 'N new lines since you last closed the Records, K of war and peace' and 'Newest: <words> <name>, <date>' (GetTokenLocalizedKey in a tooltip); Close clears both",
    "mod1440_chk_old3 (a save of before the review), then the Records opened: mod1440_chk_sizes3 reads every log's n as long as its dates; no line is on the lighter band; no 'Left the service' line for an officer gone before",
    "error.log: no line that names the mod, no 'invalid scope for var', no 'Could not find sprite type', no unknown trigger has_war_with",
    "E7 with Road to 56: after mod1440_chk_e7_generals (Himmler, Bormann, Canaris get a command) and one day, the 'Commissioned' lines: each officer's face beside his name is his own, the same as in the game's commander picker (Himmler: Road to 56's texture file; Canaris: his civilian portrait, accepted by the user), not the unknown leader",
    "E7: a state taken with a general on the spot: Keitel given Army 1 (in Brandenburg), mod1440_chk_war, then mod1440_chk_e7_take (Army 1's divisions moved to Poznan, which Germany then takes; game.log 'MOD1440 e7 take: N German divisions'): the line 'State taken Poznan' names Keitel in the Officer column with his own face (Road to 56's texture file), the same as in his army's leader view. No general on the line: mod1440_chk_e7_take_again (Poland takes it back, Germany again)",
    "E7: the faces sit exactly on their lines (no offset, none on a line without an officer) while the list scrolls with the wheel and the scrollbar; a click on an officer's face or name still opens his file; mod1440_chk_e7_log lists one face per officer line",
    "E7: an officer who left the service (mod1440_chk_e7_retire after choosing him on the Officers page, then one day): his 'Left the service' line shows the table's portrait or the unknown leader, never an empty spot"
  ],
